Implements migration `0013_projection_invalidation_recompute` and the next safety layer for derived student-profile data.

- automatically registers causal dependency edges for Error/Success observations, selected profile inputs, recommendations and session-plan usage;
- introduces `invalidation_batch` plus per-descendant `invalidation_record` depth without deleting or rewriting historical generations;
- marks affected StudentProfileSnapshot history as stale and downstream Recommendation history as invalidated;
- registers materialized projection outputs and queues recomputation only for the currently selected generation, leaving historical generations intact;
- coalesces repeated invalidations for the same active projection scope into one durable request while retaining every causal link;
- adds guarded claim/fail/retry/complete queue lifecycle with append-only state-event history;
- requires a successful completed ProjectionRun to be atomically activated before a recompute request can be completed;
- exposes a read-only `current_student_profile_status` view so callers can distinguish a current-but-stale profile while recomputation is pending;
- removes direct worker DML on invalidation/recompute tables and routes state changes through SECURITY DEFINER functions;
- adds `008_projection_invalidation_recompute.sql` plus updated runtime permission tests.

No source/original Google Drive file is moved, renamed, edited, deleted or permission-changed. No bridge scoring/mastery formula is introduced by this layer.

