`pkg/parser/schema_suggestions.go` had two independent implementations of the same YAML scalar extraction strategy — one inlined in `extractTopLevelYAMLValue`, one in `buildNestedYAMLScalarMatchers`/`extractNestedYAMLScalar` — both covering the same three value forms (single-quoted, double-quoted, unquoted with trailing-comment trimming) with the same `FindStringSubmatch`/`TrimSpace` flow.

### Changes

- **Shared matcher construction**: added `yamlScalarValueForms` (the three value patterns) plus `buildYAMLScalarMatchers(keyPrefix)` and `matchYAMLScalar(content, matchers)`. The only difference between the two call sites is now the key prefix.
- **Top-level extraction**: `extractTopLevelYAMLValue` collapses from ~30 lines of repeated compile/match blocks to a prefix + delegate, keeping the column-0 anchor.
- **Nested extraction**: `extractNestedYAMLValue` reuses the shared helpers; the nested-only `buildNestedYAMLScalarMatchers` and `extractNestedYAMLScalar` are removed. Block-scanning and indent logic are untouched.
- **Test**: added a top-level unquoted-value-with-inline-comment case to `TestExtractYAMLValueAtPath`, which previously only exercised that form on the nested path.

```go
func extractTopLevelYAMLValue(yamlContent, fieldName string) string {
	// Anchor to column 0 (no leading whitespace) so nested keys with the same name are not matched.
	matchers, err := buildYAMLScalarMatchers(`(?m)^` + regexp.QuoteMeta(fieldName) + `[ \t]*:[ \t]*`)
	if err != nil {
		return ""
	}
	return matchYAMLScalar(yamlContent, matchers)
}
```

Matcher ordering (quoted before unquoted) and per-form regexes are unchanged, so extraction results should be identical.

